# Fear of Falling (4/4 flying): "Whenever this creature attacks, target creature defending player controls gets -2/-0 and loses flying until your next turn."
# Bot2 has a Wind Drake and an Ornithopter, so the ability asks which: Bot1's own Fear of Falling is refused (it is not a creature defending player controls),
# Bot2's Wind Drake is accepted and becomes 0/2 without flying, and the Ornithopter is untouched. The effect outlasts the turn (CR 611.2a): on turn 4 the Drake
# is still 0/2 and grounded, and on turn 5, when Bot1's next turn begins, it is a 2/2 flier again. Fear of Falling, unblocked by the grounded Drake, deals 4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Fear of Falling
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Wind Drake
Ornithopter
Island x4
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fear of Falling.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Wind Drake.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Keywords = Flying
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Fear of Falling > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Fear of Falling)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Power = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Toughness = 2
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Keywords = (absent)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 16
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Power = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Keywords = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Power = 2
[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Keywords = Flying
Bot2.Battlefield.Wind Drake.Toughness = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
